#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:2518
msgid "Per-form settings — exclusion, URL parameters, headers, notification rules — key these submissions as <code>custom:&lt;form_id&gt;</code> when you pass a <code>form_id</code>, and <code>custom:&lt;form_name&gt;</code> when you do not. Passing a stable <code>form_id</code> is therefore what lets you rename the form later without resetting its configuration."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:2522
msgid "Submission fields — id, label, value"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:2524
msgid "<strong>Two shapes are accepted, and both are fully supported.</strong> The richer descriptor list is preferred; the historical map is not deprecated."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:2525
msgid "(a) Descriptor list — preferred"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:2526
msgid "An ordered list of <code>{id, label, value}</code> arrays, matching the <a href=\"#payloads\"><code>submission_data</code> schema 2.0</a> wire format one-for-one:"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:2538
msgid "The field's stable, machine-readable identifier — what a receiver should match on. Passed through <code>sanitize_text_field()</code>. An entry whose <code>id</code> is empty after sanitizing is <strong>dropped</strong>, as is any <code>id</code> beginning with <code>cvm_</code> in any letter case."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:2539
msgid "The human-readable label — what a person reads in the Submissions panel, a CSV export, or a notification email. Sanitized the same way, and <strong>falls back to <code>id</code></strong> when missing, blank, or not a scalar."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:2540
msgid "A scalar (cast to string) or a <strong>list of scalars</strong>, each sanitized. Arrays are reindexed with <code>array_values()</code>, so a multi-select's own keys are not part of the contract. Anything non-scalar — an object, a nested array — becomes an empty string rather than nested data. A missing <code>value</code> is an empty string."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:2541
msgid "(b) name =&gt; value map — the long-standing shape"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:2542
msgid "Every key becomes both the field's <code>id</code> <strong>and</strong> its <code>label</code>:"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:2556
msgid "That is the only difference between the two shapes: the map cannot express a label distinct from the id. Use it when you have no separate label to give; reach for the descriptor list the moment you do."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:2557
msgid "<strong>Shape detection is strict, and deliberately so.</strong> An array is treated as a descriptor list only when it is list-keyed <em>and every entry</em> is an array carrying a scalar <code>id</code>. One entry that fails sends the whole array down the map path, where nothing is lost — a permissive test that sniffed only the first entry would misread a map whose values happen to be arrays with an <code>id</code> key and silently discard your data."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:2558
msgid "Rules that apply to both shapes"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:2560
msgid "<strong><code>cvm_*</code> keys are always stripped</strong>, from either shape, in any letter case. Convermetry's correlation fields never reach storage, payloads, exports, emails, or the Activity Log."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:2561
msgid "<strong>Duplicate labels are preserved as separate fields.</strong> Nothing keys or deduplicates by label; two fields both labelled \"Name\" stay two fields. This is the whole reason the wire format is a list."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:2562
msgid "<strong>Order is preserved</strong> exactly as you passed it."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:2563
msgid "<strong>An empty field list is valid</strong> — it records a submission with an empty schema 2.0 list, not a legacy-shaped payload."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:2564
msgid "Values are <strong>sanitized, never validated</strong>. Convermetry is not your form's validator; it records what the form accepted."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:2568
